CHAPTER IX
MINIMUM SERVICE STANDARDS
Article 26
(1) The Regency Government shall formulate Minimum Service Standards for protection activities for women and children victims of violence and human trafficking.
(2) The Minimum Service Standards as referred to in paragraph (1), shall include services for:
a. handling complaints/reports of victims of violence against women and children;
b. health services for women and children victims of violence;
c. social rehabilitation for women and children victims of violence;
d. law enforcement and legal assistance for women and children victims of violence; and
e. repatriation and social reintegration for women and children victims of violence.

Article 12
Forms of services for victims organized by P2TP2A include:
a. medical services, in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of victims carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. medicolegal services constitute a form of medical service for the purpose of evidence in the legal field;
c. psychosocial services constitute services provided by companions in order to restore the traumatic condition of victims, including the provision of safe houses to protect victims from various forms of threats and intimidation against victims and to provide social support so that victims have self-confidence, strength, and independence in resolving their problems;
d. legal services are services to assist victims in carrying out the judicial process;
e. economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and providing economic access so that victims can be independent;
f. spiritual services include providing explanations about rights, obligations and strengthening of faith and piety;
g. continuous services at the rehabilitation and reintegration stage.

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF BANYUWANGI,

Considering : a. that violence against women and children as well as trafficking in persons constitutes an act of degrading human dignity and degree, therefore they need to be provided with adequate services and protection;
b. that the level of trafficking in persons, violence against women and children is still high, therefore it is the obligation of the regional government to regulate and serve the interests of the community, in this case women and children victims of violence and trafficking in persons;
c. that in order for the handling of trafficking in persons, violence against women and children to be implemented effectively and efficiently, it is necessary to regulate the protection of women and children victims of violence and trafficking in persons;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a, b and c, it is necessary to establish a regional regulation on the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence and Trafficking in Persons.

In View of : 1. Law Number 12 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas within the Province of East Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 4), as amended by Law Number 2 of 1965 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1965 Number 19, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2730);
2. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1979 Number 23, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);
3. Law Number 8 of 1981 concerning Criminal Procedure Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1981 Number 76; Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3209);
4. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
5. Law Number 8 of 1985 concerning Social Organizations (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3298);
6. Law Number 3 of 1997 concerning Juvenile Court (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1997 Number 76, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);
7. Law Number 5 of 1998 Concerning Ratification of the Convention Against Torture and Other Cruel, Inhuman or Degrading Treatment or Punishment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1998 Number 164, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3783);
8. Law Number 20 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention No. 138 Concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment (ILO Convention concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 56, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);
9. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
10. Law Number 1 of 2000 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention No. 182 Concerning The Prohibition and Immediate Action for The Elimination of The Worst Forms of Child Labour (ILO Convention Number 182 concerning Prohibition and Immediate Action for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labour (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2000 Number 30, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3941);
11. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3941);
12. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);
13. Law Number 10 of 2004 concerning Establishment of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 53, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4389);
14. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
15. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as last amended by Law Number 12 of 2008 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 108, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4548);
16. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
17. Law Number 11 of 2009 Concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4967);
18. Government Regulation Number 27 of 1983 concerning Implementation of the Criminal Procedure Code, as amended by Government Regulation Number 58 of 2010 concerning Amendment to Government Regulation Number 90 of 2010 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 112, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5145);
19. Government Regulation of the Republic of Indonesia Number 79 of 2005 concerning Guidelines for Development and Supervision of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2005 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4593);
20. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
21. Government Regulation Number 9 of 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);
22. Government Regulation Number 44 of 2008 concerning Provision of Compensation, Restitution and Assistance to Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 84, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4860);
23. Presidential Regulation Number 1 of 2007 concerning Ratification, Promulgation and Dissemination of Legislation.
24. Presidential Regulation of the Republic of Indonesia Number 69 of 2008 Concerning Task Force for Prevention and Handling of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons.
25. Regional Regulation of East Java Province Number 9 of 2005 concerning Implementation of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence and Trafficking in Persons (Regional Gazette of East Java Province Year 2005 Number 4 Series E);

With the Mutual Approval of
THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BANYUWANGI REGENCY
